# ── Secrets — NEVER commit these ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# ── User data / runtime state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. An unanchored `data/` matches a
# directory named `data` at ANY depth — which silently swallowed the entire
# GEV data-layer source tree (src/gev/js/data/: 114 modules + ~100 test files).
# Because gitignore only applies to UNTRACKED files, that tree was never
# committed, so CI checked out a GEV app missing its own data layer:
# scripts/gev/run-unit-tests.mjs died on "Missing allocation microbenchmarks",
# `npm test` silently ran 44 of ~144 GEV suites, and any tracked module that
# imports ../data/*.js could not resolve on a clean checkout.
# Nested runtime-data dirs are listed explicitly instead — one rule per real
# runtime dir. Do NOT reintroduce a bare `data/`: it is fail-silent (source
# disappears, CI breaks) whereas an unlisted new dir fails open (shows up in
# git status, reviewable). Re-verify with:
#   git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard | grep '/data/'
/data/
server/data/
server/systems/data/
# GEV dataset cache — fetched/derived at runtime, referenced by no source file.
src/gev/js/data/local_data/
# Downloaded design-corpus payload (the tracked siblings are scripts/*.py).
.shared/ui-ux-pro-max/data/
# Sub-project runtime state (users/, federated/, learning/ — read by no code).
pulse-news/backend/data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
trust_states.json
identity_*.json
agent_registry.json
episodic/
vault/
*.ndjson

